      "type": "textEditor",
      "data": {
        "value": "<p><strong>IHC No- 518/2024</strong><br><strong>Gross :-&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>Received paraffin tissue block No. <strong>MDRC, 20865/24</strong><br><strong>Clinical Details :</strong><br><br><strong>IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY RESULTS</strong></p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>IHC MARKER(S)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; RESULT</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CD 34</td>\n<td>Occasional immature cells are highlighted. No clusters of positive cells seen. Overall percentage is less than 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CD 117</td>\n<td>Some mast cells and plasma cells are highlighted along with occasional immature cells. No clusters of positive cells identified.&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><br><strong>IMPRESSION: No definite increase in immature cells identified on immunohistochemistry</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;<strong>Notes :</strong><br>&nbsp;1.&nbsp;This test was performed on paraffin embedded tissue section.<br>2.&nbsp;Detection system used &ndash; Biogenex &nbsp;Real Envision Detection system, peroxidase/ DAB + Rabbit/mouse.<br>3.&nbsp;The impression is based on the material submitted and is not a complete surgical pathlogy report.<br>4.&nbsp;Improper Fixation may affect results.&nbsp;<br><br>&nbsp;<strong>Fixative requirement :</strong><br>&nbsp;1.&nbsp;The volume of formalin fixative should be atleast 10 times the volume of the specimen<br>2.&nbsp;Specimens should be immersed in 10% neutral buffered formalin within 1 hours of the biopsy/ resection procedure ( time of removal&nbsp;and time of immersion to be mentioned )<br>3. In all resection (large) specimens , the tumour must be bisected prior to immersion in fixative.</p>",
        "field": "textEditor"
      },
      "_id": "6798c9d625c8f713dff0cd28"
    }
